# --- vibe-forge baseline .env.example ---------------------------------------
# This file is a PLACEHOLDER. The real stack-specific .env.example will be
# generated by INIT_PROMPT after the interview, copied from one of the
# templates in templates/env-examples/ (supabase / firebase / postgres /
# vercel / custom) and tailored to the user's answers.
#
# DO NOT commit a real .env file. Only .env.example should be tracked.
#
# Conventions used across all generated env files:
#   - UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for variable names
#   - Public/client-side keys prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_, VITE_, PUBLIC_, etc.
#   - Server-only secrets never prefixed with a public marker
#   - Each variable has a one-line comment above it explaining purpose,
#     where to obtain it, and whether it is required or optional.

